     "text": "```json\n{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Block mailClient:exploitPublicApp, codeRepo:collection and mailArchive:collection. Without mailClient, vpnSession:authenticate cannot be reached. That cuts hypervisor:privilegeEscalation, and with it vaultRead:collection. It also cuts serviceAccount:privilegeEscalation, and with it dbReplica:collection. codeRepo:collection is blocked directly, even though printServer:lateralMovement stays reachable via sshKey:credentialAccess. mailArchive:collection is blocked directly, even though monitoringHost:lateralMovement stays reachable via exposedApi:initialAccess -> tokenCache:credentialAccess. Two blocks are not enough because three attack chains share no blockable step. Chain 1: exposedApi -> tokenCache -> monitoringHost -> mailArchive. Chain 2: internet -> sshKey -> printServer -> codeRepo. Chain 3: browserStore + mailClient -> vpnSession -> hypervisor -> vaultRead. Each of these chains needs its own block.\"}\n```"
